other tiles.\n\nAnother option is to discard W9. Since it's a terminal and not part of any chow, it's safe. But if they discard W9, they might have to rely on other tiles for a pair. However, keeping F2 for Seat Wind is better.\n\nSo the best move is to discard F1.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The best move is to discard F1 as it is an honor tile not part of any chow and not the player's seat wind (South Wind), minimizing the risk of aiding opponents while preserving potential for future melds.\nReason: Discarding F1 avoids giving opponents a chance to complete a pung of East Wind (F1 is the prevailing wind) and preserves the seat wind tile F2 for potential Seat Wind points. This maintains the possibility of forming a concealed hand with multiple chows (B3-B4-B5 and T6-T7-T8) and a pair, while avoiding high-value discard risks.\nAnswer: Play F1"}
